#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:801
msgid "Resource dimensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:805
msgid ""
"The [GetDimensions] DXIL operation returns the dimensions of a texture or "
"buffer resource. It returns a [Dimensions] type, which is a struct "
"containing four `i32` values. The values in the struct represent the size of "
"each dimension of the resource, and when aplicable the number of array "
"elements or number of samples. The mapping is defined in the [GetDimensions] "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:812
msgid ""
"The LLVM IR representation of this operation has several forms depending on "
"the resource type and the specific `getDimensions` query. The intrinsics "
"return a scalar or anonymous struct with up to 4 `i32` elements. The "
"intrinsic names include suffixes to indicate the number of elements in the "
"return value. The suffix `.x` indicates a single `i32` return value, `.xy` "
"indicates a struct with two `i32` values, and `.xyz` indicates a struct with "
"three `i32` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:820
msgid ""
"Intrinsics representing queries on multisampled texture resources include `."
"ms.` in their name and their return value includes an additional `i32` for "
"the number of samples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:824
msgid ""
"Intrinsics with `mip_level` argument and `.levels.` in their name are used "
"for texture resources with multiple MIP levels. Their return struct includes "
"an additional `i32` for the number of levels the resource has."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:839
msgid "`@llvm.dx.resource.getdimensions.*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:848
msgid "`i32`, `{i32, i32}`, `{i32, i32, i32}`, or `{i32, i32, i32, i32}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../DirectX/DXILResources.md:849
msgid ""
"Width, height, and depth of the resource (based on the specific suffix), and "
"a number of levels or samples where aplicable."
msgstr ""

